A||||7||la9||Vacuum Canister||||1||
Z||000000||la9||03-06-2000||12:10 AM||||Can you buy a new vacuum canister at the normal autoparts stores or do you have to order one from GM ???? There is a hole the size of my fist rusted in mine, I hope this is why my cruise isn't working.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Earne||03-06-2000||12:38 AM||||Don't know if there are any generic canisters out there but three local GM dealerships say that I bought the last one from a GM dealer near Toronto.  Took several weeks to get and the shipping was more than the canister.  I'm sure more will turn up, the GM parts database is not foolproof.  Things, especially older things sometimes don't get inventoried.  Then they are found later and put back on the computer.  I would keep checking periodically.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-06-2000||06:47 AM||||Are you talking about the coffee can size thingy if so just use a tin can.||||reg||1
Z||000003||William Federle||03-06-2000||06:51 AM||||The Fiero Store has them for $49.00<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||03-06-2000||09:55 AM||||I fashioned one from a juice can (same size as the original vacuum canister). So far it's working perfectly <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||la9||03-06-2000||10:52 AM||||How did you put the fitting on so it wouldn't leak ?||||reg||1
Z||000006||GWMORGAN||03-06-2000||01:39 PM||||la9...I took the vacuum "nipples" from the old canister, then cut a hole in one end of the juics can (I drank the juice of course)and glued the "nipples" over the hole using an eletrical glue gun. Before installing, I sprayed the can with rust prevention paint. It's been working fine for the past 6k miles.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||03-06-2000||08:06 PM||||You can get new canisters. Get one of the plastic ball ones. They look better and don't rust.<P>The MotorMite master catalog has them. You can also get one off practically anything at the local scrap yard for about a dollar if they even charge you for it. If you get a used one make sure the check valve works is all.<P>Size of the canister isn't real critical. Anything close to the same size as the original one will work. For Fiero the grapefruit sized ones are probably large enough. It's only there for backup vacuum for the cruise unit.||||reg||1
